### ❌ Critical Errors (Config Test Will Fail)

| Line | Issue | Correct Directive |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `server {` | **Missing `http` context.** `server` blocks must live inside `http { ... }`. | Wrap in `http { ... }` |
| `server_name localhost;` | **Directive does not exist.** | `server_name localhost;` |
| `proxy_pass ...` | **Directive does not exist.** | `proxy_pass ...` |

---

### ✅ Corrected & Production-Ready Version

```nginx
# 1. Required context wrapper
http {
    # 2. Upstream block (recommended for maintainability/health checks)
    upstream backend_app {
        server <IP_ADDRESS>:3000;  # Replace <IP_ADDRESS> with actual IP or hostname
        # server 10.0.0.5:3000 backup; # Optional: backup server
        keepalive 32;              # Connection pooling to upstream
    }

    server {
        listen 8080;
        server_name localhost;

        # 3. Security: Hide Nginx version
        server_tokens off;

        # 4. Buffer sizing (prevents 502 Bad Gateway on large headers)
        proxy_buffer_size          128k;
        proxy_buffers              4 256k;
        proxy_busy_buffers_size    256k;
        proxy_busy_buffers         4;

        location / {
            # 5. Correct directive name
            proxy_pass http://backend_app;

            # 6. ESSENTIAL: Pass client info to backend
            proxy_set_header Host $host;
            proxy_set_header X-Real-IP $remote_addr;
            proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;
            proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Proto $scheme;
            proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Host $host;
            proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Port $server_port;

            # 7. WebSocket Support (if needed)
            proxy_set_header Upgrade $http_upgrade;
            proxy_set_header Connection "upgrade";

            # 8. Timeouts (tune per app requirements)
            proxy_connect_timeout  5s;
            proxy_send_timeout     60s;
            proxy_read_timeout     60s;

            # 9. Buffering control (off for streaming/large uploads)
            # proxy_request_buffering off;
            # proxy_buffering off;
        }

        # 10. Health check endpoint (exclude from logs)
        location /health {
            access_log off;
            return 200 "healthy\n";
        }
    }
}
```

---

### 🔑 Key Fixes & Additions Explained

| # | Change | Why It Matters |
|:-:| :--- | :--- |
| **1** | `http { ... }` | Nginx requires `server` blocks inside `http` (or `stream`/`mail`). Top-level `server` is invalid. |
| **2** | `upstream` block | Decouples IP/port from logic. Enables load balancing, health checks (`match`), and easier DNS updates. |
| **3** | `server_tokens off` | Security hygiene: removes `Server: nginx/x.x.x` header. |
| **4** | `proxy_buffer*` | Default buffers (4k/8k) are tiny. Large cookies/headers from modern apps (SPAs, auth tokens) cause `502` errors without this. |
| **6** | `proxy_set_header` | **Critical.** Backend sees `127.0.0.1` without `X-Real-IP`/`X-Forwarded-For`. Breaks rate limiting, logging, auth, geo-IP. |
| **7** | `Upgrade`/`Connection` | Required for WebSockets / Server-Sent Events (SSE) / gRPC-Web. Safe to leave on always. |
| **8** | Explicit Timeouts | Defaults (60s) are okay, but explicit docs intent. `connect_timeout` low fails fast if upstream down. |
| **9** | Buffering Flags | `proxy_buffering off` sends response flush-by-flush (streaming). `proxy_request_buffering off` streams upload to backend. |
| **10** | `/health` | Standard LB/k8s probe target. `access_log off` keeps logs clean. |

